ntent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR."}}}, {"asked": "the opt-out and frequency floor", "found": "opt-in/opt-out and fatigue control", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 84, "end": 86, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d35c7c8b4930ee9b9b1e6980bedfb085afb88d32897894e337afaf6be756e35", "text": "  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference \u2014 when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 81, "end": 89, "text": "  - Level 2 \u2014 in-session experience-nudge vs channel-bell: present \u2192 hand to `experience`'s nudge layer; away \u2192 fire the channel. Add when real-time presence signals are reliable.\n  - Level 3 \u2014 player-type tailoring: shape the nudge to gami