 click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}, {"asked": "frequency discipline", "found": "cap low-value sends to protect attention; never spam", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 86, "end": 86, "fingerprint": "sha256:a4474b468e9c9ecc8f91c6965b7b726a14be2246873b8c11beaf166c1a8819e5", "text": "  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 83, "end": 89, "text": "- **Preferences & frequency** \u2014 let the user stay in control; never spam.\n  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference \u2014 when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.\n\n## Where it goes wrong\n- **Fatigue & noise** \u2014 too many low-value messages; no frequency discipline."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-019", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Where does the reminder's link take the customer?", "answer": "Back to the same cart on the shop's normal cart page and checkout path, never a side path", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the core journey", "found": "home -> category -> PLP -> PDP -> cart -> checkout handoff must always be present", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 83, "end": 91, "fingerprint": "sha256:83a5a3ee99653346ea5f35e5b2a130adbdce626294a2ea3fe0c570fd404a909e", "text": "## The core journey \u2014 always there, or it breaks\nStart with the basics and make sure the core is always present. Without it the\njourney breaks, no matter the quadrant:\n\n**home \u2192 category pages \u2192 PLP (product listing) \u2192 PDP (product detail) \u2192 cart \u2192\ncheckout handoff.**\n\nBuild this spine first, end to end, before any enrichment. Everything else hangs\noff it.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 80, "end": 94, "text": "not where we lead. Keep them on the spectrum so the choice is honest; just know\nwhich engagements are ours to drive and which we route elsewhere.\n\n## The core journey \u2014 always there, or it breaks\nStart with the basics and make sure the core is always present. Without it the\njourney breaks, no matter the quadrant:\n\n**home \u2192 category pages \u2192 PLP (product listing) \u2192 PDP (product detail) \u2192 cart \u2192\ncheckout handoff.**\n\nBuild this spine first, end to end, before any enrichment. Everything else hangs\noff it.\n\n## Capabilities (after the spine, selected by quadrant)\n- **Product content & SKU management** \u2014 the big variable. WHERE it lives is set"}}}, {"asked": "the cart reminder link", "found": "a link that restores the same cart", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:758279c57f70d4f95e014931f0c4cefdde307dab095d65515c44cf910b130366", "text": "  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-020", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What may the reminder message say?", "answer": "A helpful note in the shop's voice; no offer, false urgency or scarcity; always a one-click opt-out", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "allowed and forbidden nudges", "found": "helpful reminders allowed; dark patterns (deceptive urgency, manipulative scarcity, consent bypass) forbidden", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/experience.md", "start": 76, "end": 81, "fingerprint": "sha256:7bcf42bba60295a5c3a1b7d32eb190ed80291c490e16e6239f53b074a7357fb7", "text": "A **nudge is a governed intervention** \u2014 trigger signal, message, channel,\nconfidence, expected outcome, guardrail policy \u2014 and **every nudge must be\nmeasurable**. Allowed: progress visibility, completion cues, milestones, helpful\nreminders, choice simplification, confidence-building explanations, recovery\nnudges. **Forbidden: dark patterns** \u2014 deceptive urgency, hidden opt-ins,\nmanipulative scarcity, pressure loops, consent bypass. When confidence drops or", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 73, "end": 84, "text": "backtracking, repeated comparison, unresolved loops, high-intent page depth,\nfrustration language, stalled journey stage.\n\nA **nudge is a governed intervention** \u2014 trigger signal, message, channel,\nconfidence, expected outcome, guardrail policy \u2014 and **every nudge must be\nmeasurable**. Allowed: progress visibility, completion cues, milestones, helpful\nreminders, choice simplification, confidence-building explanations, recovery\nnudges. **Forbidden: dark patterns** \u2014 deceptive urgency, hidden opt-ins,\nmanipulative scarcity, pressure loops, consent bypass. When confidence drops or\nrisk rises, **escalate to a human**. This is in-session intelligence \u2014 not CDP\npersonalisation.\n"}}}, {"asked": "consent on reach", "found": "opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach activity", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/marketing.md", "start": 73, "end": 75, "fingerprint": "sha256:14acbcf9a1a92d93ae21122a4e23f966c51c3b05b6fbba883da5af4c6bc184b3", "text": "  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 70, "end": 78, "text": "  - GEO \u2014 be surfaced by generative engines. Add as generative reach grows.\n  - Agent-visibility \u2014 be readable by agents crawling on a user's behalf. Add when\n    agent-driven discovery is part of the channel mix.\n  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.\n- **Campaign page production** \u2014 include when campaigns need landing pages.\n  Progressive (maturity ladder \u2014 climb as volume and reuse grow):\n  - Level 1 \u2014 single campaign page stood up fast on the MACH / drag-and-drop spine."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-021", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Which channel carries the reminder?", "answer": "Email, via the notifications side", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "away-from-app channel for a web product", "found": "Email when surfaces include web/api and durable away-from-app reach is needed", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 70, "end": 74, "fingerprint": "sha256:f01076e9c9917deaba623bb647ac0d2a242fd3d53ab10e92682fa074dc39fa77", "text": "- **Channel delivery** \u2014 reach the user wherever they are. Multi-channel is the\n  floor, not a stretch (flat list \u2014 channels are independent, add per surface).\n  - In-app \u2014 the floor; messages and badges inside the product (`shape.surfaces` includes web/mobile/desktop).\n  - Push \u2014 when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile (or web with push support) and timely re-engagement matters.\n  - Email \u2014 when `shape.surfaces` includes web/api and you need durable, away-from-app reach.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 67, "end": 77, "text": "floor; add only when a profile dimension calls for it. These serve the POV above \u2014\nthey do not replace it.\n\n- **Channel delivery** \u2014 reach the user wherever they are. Multi-channel is the\n  floor, not a stretch (flat list \u2014 channels are independent, add per surface).\n  - In-app \u2014 the floor; messages and badges inside the product (`shape.surfaces` includes web/mobile/desktop).\n  - Push \u2014 when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile (or web with push support) and timely re-engagement matters.\n  - Email \u2014 when `shape.surfaces` includes web/api and you need durable, away-from-app reach.\n  - SMS \u2014 when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile and reach must not depend on app/email; add `nfr.privacy >= high` care for phone numbers.\n- **Templating** \u2014 one message, channel-appropriate renderings, authored via the experience layer.\n  - Per-channel templates \u2014 the floor once more than one channel exists; one message, channel-specific rendering composed where the experience is."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-022", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What NFR levels does abandoned-cart-reminders need?", "answer": "privacy high; reliability, performance, security, observability medium", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "privacy care for contact", "found": "opt-in is the floor at privacy >= medium; consent gaps are a named failure", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 84, "end": 92, "fingerprint": "sha256:ba8b262f63d44699b78a2647947fb399f91c2382296740c84f574335c5b7c5b2", "text": "  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference \u2014 when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.\n\n## Where it goes wrong\n- **Fatigue & noise** \u2014 too many low-value messages; no frequency discipline.\n- **Wrong channel** \u2014 bell when an in-session experience nudge would have been better;\n  or a channel the user didn't want.\n- **Consent & preference gaps** \u2014 ignoring opt-in/opt-out and per-channel preference.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 81, "end": 95, "text": "  - Level 2 \u2014 in-session experience-nudge vs channel-bell: present \u2192 hand to `experience`'s nudge layer; away \u2192 fire the channel. Add when real-time presence signals are reliable.\n  - Level 3 \u2014 player-type tailoring: shape the nudge to gamified behaviour (progress/achievement/exploration/social). Add when `personalization` supplies a behavioural profile.\n- **Preferences & frequency** \u2014 let the user stay in control; never spam.\n  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference \u2014 when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.\n\n## Where it goes wrong\n- **Fatigue & noise** \u2014 too many low-value messages; no frequency discipline.\n- **Wrong channel** \u2014 bell when an in-session experience nudge would have been better;\n  or a channel the user didn't want.\n- **Consent & preference gaps** \u2014 ignoring opt-in/opt-out and per-channel preference.\n- **Brand-tone drift** \u2014 inconsistent voice across channels.\n- **One-size nudging** \u2014 ignoring player type, so motivation misfires.\n"}}}, {"asked": "consent on reach", "found": "never ship reach without consent and opt-out", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/marketing.md", "start": 73, "end": 75, "fingerprint": "sha256:14acbcf9a1a92d93ae21122a4e23f966c51c3b05b6fbba883da5af4c6bc184b3", "text": "  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 70, "end": 78, "text": "  - GEO \u2014 be surfaced by generative engines. Add as generative reach grows.\n  - Agent-visibility \u2014 be readable by agents crawling on a user's behalf. Add when\n    agent-driven discovery is part of the channel mix.\n  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.\n- **Campaign page production** \u2014 include when campaigns need landing pages.\n  Progressive (maturity ladder \u2014 climb as volume and reuse grow):\n  - Level 1 \u2014 single campaign page stood up fast on the MACH / drag-and-drop spine."}}}, {"asked": "requirement in the approved node", "found": "requires opt-in where privacy >= medium or compliance includes GDPR", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:758279c57f70d4f95e014931f0c4cefdde307dab095d65515c44cf910b130366", "text": "  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-023", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Which compliance regimes does abandoned-cart-reminders trigger?", "answer": "None listed yet; regions unknown, raised as memory update mu-20261020-005; opt-in and opt-out enforced regardless", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "regimes governing consent for reach", "found": "GDPR / CAN-SPAM named, but which applies depends on regions no tier records", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/marketing.md", "start": 73, "end": 75, "fingerprint": "sha256:14acbcf9a1a92d93ae21122a4e23f966c51c3b05b6fbba883da5af4c6bc184b3", "text": "  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 70, "end": 78, "text": "  - GEO \u2014 be surfaced by generative engines. Add as generative reach grows.\n  - Agent-visibility \u2014 be readable by agents crawling on a user's behalf. Add when\n    agent-driven discovery is part of the channel mix.\n  - Consent & privacy for reach \u2014 opt-in, opt-out, suppression on any reach\n    activity. The floor whenever `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes\n    GDPR / CAN-SPAM; never ship reach without it.\n- **Campaign page production** \u2014 include when campaigns need landing pages.\n  Progressive (maturity ladder \u2014 climb as volume and reuse grow):\n  - Level 1 \u2014 single campaign page stood up fast on the MACH / drag-and-drop spine."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-024", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Where in the knowledge base does the carts-won-back capability belong?", "answer": "Analytics (Goals, Product-conversion funnel, Fixed dashboards, meaningful product events), reading ecommerce order records; the approved abandoned-cart recovery answer names it Recovery tracking and sends measurement to analytics.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:57:01Z", "trace": [{"asked": "which shelf owns measuring an outcome against a goal", "found": "analytics: measurement answers did the intended outcome happen; tie behaviour to outcome", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 23, "end": 24, "fingerprint": "sha256:a5979317297c2868a346dcb525a03a8f83ff63b8a159ffdb31821ade939a5b36", "text": "Intent-first: measurement exists to answer \"did the intended outcome happen, and\nwhere did people fall out.\" Couple it to decisions or don't bother.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 20, "end": 27, "text": "- **Measure product analytics, not just web.** Feature usage, adoption, retention,\n  cohorts \u2014 the product, not only the marketing site.\n\nIntent-first: measurement exists to answer \"did the intended outcome happen, and\nwhere did people fall out.\" Couple it to decisions or don't bother.\n\n## Two kinds of funnel \u2014 don't conflate them\nThis matters because `experience` says funnels are the *wrong* lens \u2014 that's a"}}}, {"asked": "the analytics capability for a named success outcome", "found": "Goal definition is the floor", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 61, "end": 61, "fingerprint": "sha256:33c99c5ad97399ba79d64f0524353581b8a106edc0ead50080171819c70a6f05", "text": "  - Goal definition \u2014 name the success outcome and its event. The floor \u2014 without it you measure motion, not value.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 58, "end": 64, "text": "  - Level 2 \u2014 meaningful product events: the few actions that mean something (signup, activate, convert). Add when the product has a goal to measure against.\n  - Level 3 \u2014 full event taxonomy: named events with consistent properties, versioned. Add when `nfr.maintainability >= high` or multiple teams emit events.\n- **Goals** \u2014 explicit success definitions, the spine of value.\n  - Goal definition \u2014 name the success outcome and its event. The floor \u2014 without it you measure motion, not value.\n  - Goal hierarchy \u2014 primary vs assist goals, weighted. Add when one surface drives several outcomes worth ranking.\n- **Funnels** \u2014 product/conversion funnels with drop-off, not discovery funnels.\n  - Product-conversion funnel \u2014 the in-product path to a goal (signup \u2192 activate \u2192 convert \u2192 retain) with drop-off at each step. The floor for this shelf."}}}, {"asked": "the funnel for abandoned to reminded to ordered", "found": "product-conversion funnel is the floor", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 64, "end": 64, "fingerprint": "sha256:43460344a1a5eaa4af9f673b59a12af5bc21245cfb74c7ddf8a1bb6b26b4dcd9", "text": "  - Product-conversion funnel \u2014 the in-product path to a goal (signup \u2192 activate \u2192 convert \u2192 retain) with drop-off at each step. The floor for this shelf.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 61, "end": 67, "text": "  - Goal definition \u2014 name the success outcome and its event. The floor \u2014 without it you measure motion, not value.\n  - Goal hierarchy \u2014 primary vs assist goals, weighted. Add when one surface drives several outcomes worth ranking.\n- **Funnels** \u2014 product/conversion funnels with drop-off, not discovery funnels.\n  - Product-conversion funnel \u2014 the in-product path to a goal (signup \u2192 activate \u2192 convert \u2192 retain) with drop-off at each step. The floor for this shelf.\n  - Segmented funnel \u2014 same funnel split by cohort or property to locate where which users fall out. Add when one funnel hides divergent behaviour.\n- **Product analytics** \u2014 feature usage, adoption, retention, cohorts, paths.\n  - Feature usage & adoption \u2014 who uses which feature and how often. The floor for measuring the product, not just the site."}}}, {"asked": "what the recovery capability says about measuring the win-back", "found": "measuring the win-back is analytics (conversion funnel)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 7, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:7ee8529722f4c4554186296a6070abcc11b139a8b5ba226fb6a3a50720dcad64", "text": "  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 11, "text": "  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR."}}}, {"asked": "where the order records come from", "found": "basic stock and orders, the floor every store that sells", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 127, "end": 127, "fingerprint": "sha256:fcdd39ebe93e163261c258e4d831f479a153837d6d8a0cc44e685f5717f27f3e", "text": "  - Level 1 \u2014 basic stock & orders: simple counts and order records. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 124, "end": 130, "text": "  - Review intelligence \u2014 AI summaries and consumer review Q&A on the PDP (see intelligence). Add for public, conversion-focused storefronts.\n- **Inventory & order management** \u2014 core commerce; real-time stock when traffic\n  and reliability push (quadrants 3\u20134).\n  - Level 1 \u2014 basic stock & orders: simple counts and order records. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Level 2 \u2014 real-time stock & reservations: live availability under load. Add when `nfr.reliability >= high` and `nfr.performance >= high` (quadrants 3\u20134).\n  - Level 3 \u2014 distributed / omnichannel fulfilment: multi-warehouse, BOPIS, returns. Add when `shape.surfaces` spans channels or `nfr.scalability >= xhigh`.\n- **Integration / SOA layer** \u2014 heavy for quadrant 4: many back-end systems,"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-025", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Which functionalities does carts-won-back need?", "answer": "Four: won-back order matching, pre-reminder baseline, owner month-by-month win-back view, business win-back summary.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:57:01Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what recovery tracking must do", "found": "count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 12, "end": 12, "fingerprint": "sha256:98ba42ee5ee8d52dbbf922edb02206c2acfa24ce193dfddc862b858522b9d0ce", "text": "  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 9, "end": 14, "text": "  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}, {"asked": "how a won-back cart is recognised", "found": "the reminder link restores the same cart, so the order can be matched by cart", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:758279c57f70d4f95e014931f0c4cefdde307dab095d65515c44cf910b130366", "text": "  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}, {"asked": "what makes the comparison to before reminders possible", "found": "tie behaviour to outcome: did the change move the metric", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 47, "end": 48, "fingerprint": "sha256:767103ee3e0a08b230858d0ebdd8d4867154c0e52795bccf43a2358b206b6a98", "text": "- **Tie behaviour to outcome** \u2014 \"did the change move the metric?\" \u2192 event \u2192 goal \u2192\n  outcome (with `experience`, `personalization`, `marketing`).", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 44, "end": 51, "text": "- **See the drop-off** \u2014 \"where do people fall out on the way to the goal?\" \u2192 funnels.\n- **Understand product usage** \u2014 \"what gets used, by whom, and do they come back?\" \u2192\n  product analytics (adoption, retention, cohorts).\n- **Tie behaviour to outcome** \u2014 \"did the change move the metric?\" \u2192 event \u2192 goal \u2192\n  outcome (with `experience`, `personalization`, `marketing`).\n- **Attribute on the web** \u2014 \"credit the right source\" \u2192 web attribution (the\n  `marketing` burn \u2014 close this loop).\n"}}}, {"asked": "how the result is shown to owners and the business", "found": "fixed dashboards are the floor; self-serve only when decision cadence grows", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 78, "end": 79, "fingerprint": "sha256:ffff81db13b571744021d962a0e3b8e0b4284bc90e660417c9812ff9abd24e41", "text": "  - Fixed dashboards \u2014 the standing view of goals, funnels, usage. The floor \u2014 make the numbers legible.\n  - Self-serve exploration \u2014 ad-hoc query and breakdown without an engineer. Add when `shape.users: small-team` or more and decision cadence grows.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 75, "end": 82, "text": "  - Source/medium attribution \u2014 credit the channel that brought a session. The floor for closing the `marketing` loop.\n  - Multi-touch attribution \u2014 credit across several touches on the path to a goal. Add when `marketing` spend spans channels worth comparing.\n- **Dashboards & exploration** \u2014 make goals/funnels/usage legible and decidable.\n  - Fixed dashboards \u2014 the standing view of goals, funnels, usage. The floor \u2014 make the numbers legible.\n  - Self-serve exploration \u2014 ad-hoc query and breakdown without an engineer. Add when `shape.users: small-team` or more and decision cadence grows.\n- **Privacy-aware collection** \u2014 consent and minimisation where a regime applies.\n  - Consent gating \u2014 collect only after consent. The floor when `compliance` includes GDPR or `nfr.privacy >= medium`.\n  - Data minimisation & anonymisation \u2014 drop or hash PII, IP truncation. Add when `nfr.privacy >= high` or `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-026", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What counts as a sale won back?", "answer": "Only a placed order from the abandoned cart, at its net value; reminders sent, opened or clicked never count.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:57:01Z", "trace": [{"asked": "whether activity counts can stand in for the outcome", "found": "vanity metrics move but do not inform a decision", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 88, "end": 88, "fingerprint": "sha256:1e522ce4336426bebfd45faef7b3e8c82f9e66dc6ebccc12b0a1881565903c3d", "text": "- **Vanity metrics** \u2014 numbers that move but don't inform a decision.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 85, "end": 91, "text": "## Where it goes wrong (our gaps)\n- **Page-load + CTA only** \u2014 activity metrics with no goals or funnels \u2192 no value derived.\n- **Web only** \u2014 no product analytics, so product decisions fly blind.\n- **Vanity metrics** \u2014 numbers that move but don't inform a decision.\n- **Discovery-funnel nostalgia** \u2014 measuring a top-of-funnel LLMs now own.\n- **No attribution path on the web** \u2014 can't credit what worked.\n"}}}, {"asked": "the analytics non-negotiables", "found": "measure goals and funnels; couple measurement to decisions", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 103, "end": 105, "fingerprint": "sha256:11fbded23c70efb99eed2de01deeeb1098db8c8a2078352b4458768d37bdc959", "text": "- **Measure goals and funnels** \u2014 or you derive no value.\n- **Product analytics, not just web** \u2014 measure the product, not only the site.\n- **Couple measurement to decisions** \u2014 no vanity metrics.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 100, "end": 108, "text": "  but later than goals/funnels/product analytics, which come first.\n\n## Non-negotiables\n- **Measure goals and funnels** \u2014 or you derive no value.\n- **Product analytics, not just web** \u2014 measure the product, not only the site.\n- **Couple measurement to decisions** \u2014 no vanity metrics.\n- **Model product-conversion funnels, not discovery funnels.**\n- **Close the web-attribution loop** \u2014 the `marketing` gap.\n- **Privacy-aware collection** where a regime applies."}}}, {"asked": "how abandonment is defined", "found": "abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 9, "end": 9, "fingerprint": "sha256:03dd04430213715ba73034e24b03b316f0a19c8828734695c55160a98a78a811", "text": "  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 12, "text": "  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels)."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-027", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What NFR and compliance needs does carts-won-back set?", "answer": "reliability, observability, security and privacy at medium, performance at low; no compliance regime until a person names one (memory update mu-20261020-004 waiting).", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:57:01Z", "trace": [{"asked": "whether consent gating applies to win-back counting", "found": "consent gating is the floor when compliance includes GDPR or privacy >= medium; win-back counting collects no new shopper data, it reads existing records by cart id", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 81, "end": 81, "fingerprint": "sha256:000ad0fd76c3e30fa88040e13c1ca96e4ced09c055e59de53ac67c2b40b1be64", "text": "  - Consent gating \u2014 collect only after consent. The floor when `compliance` includes GDPR or `nfr.privacy >= medium`.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 78, "end": 84, "text": "  - Fixed dashboards \u2014 the standing view of goals, funnels, usage. The floor \u2014 make the numbers legible.\n  - Self-serve exploration \u2014 ad-hoc query and breakdown without an engineer. Add when `shape.users: small-team` or more and decision cadence grows.\n- **Privacy-aware collection** \u2014 consent and minimisation where a regime applies.\n  - Consent gating \u2014 collect only after consent. The floor when `compliance` includes GDPR or `nfr.privacy >= medium`.\n  - Data minimisation & anonymisation \u2014 drop or hash PII, IP truncation. Add when `nfr.privacy >= high` or `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA.\n  - Retention & deletion controls \u2014 TTLs and subject-deletion paths. Add when `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA / SOC2.\n"}}}, {"asked": "which events the count needs", "found": "meaningful product events, added when the product has a goal to measure against", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 58, "end": 58, "fingerprint": "sha256:26b55e9cb3bb3c78e660558c105c4a4c87f87f595b4cfa008a105268d52a192b", "text": "  - Level 2 \u2014 meaningful product events: the few actions that mean something (signup, activate, convert). Add when the product has a goal to measure against.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 55, "end": 61, "text": "## Capabilities\n- **Event tracking** \u2014 beyond page-load + CTA: meaningful product events.\n  - Level 1 \u2014 page-load + CTA clicks: the activity floor we already have, kept but never the whole story.\n  - Level 2 \u2014 meaningful product events: the few actions that mean something (signup, activate, convert). Add when the product has a goal to measure against.\n  - Level 3 \u2014 full event taxonomy: named events with consistent properties, versioned. Add when `nfr.maintainability >= high` or multiple teams emit events.\n- **Goals** \u2014 explicit success definitions, the spine of value.\n  - Goal definition \u2014 name the success outcome and its event. The floor \u2014 without it you measure motion, not value."}}}, {"asked": "whose intent the capability serves", "found": "operator Understand intent routes to analytics", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 41, "end": 41, "fingerprint": "sha256:34ed8414af7aee2120468430737f7cb2529a29600273527807a8e1b27e349796", "text": "- **Understand** \u2014 \"learn from behaviour and reviews\" \u2192 analytics, review analysis.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 38, "end": 44, "text": "**Operator (business) intents**\n- **Merchandise** \u2014 \"present and prioritise the catalog\" \u2192 merchandising, PLP curation.\n- **Enrich** \u2014 \"make products rich and on-brand\" \u2192 product content, brand-tone.\n- **Understand** \u2014 \"learn from behaviour and reviews\" \u2192 analytics, review analysis.\n- **Operate** \u2014 \"keep stock and orders flowing\" \u2192 inventory, fulfilment.\n\n## Pick the shape first (the commerce\u2194content spectrum \u2014 our POV)"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-028", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What is the Reminder record's send key built from, and which entries does its uniqueness rule cover?", "answer": "Built from shop id and cart id; at most one handed-to-delivery or sent entry per key; blocked and failed entries are not covered, so a failed send can be retried.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T05:03:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "how the send key is built", "found": "the send key is built from the shop and cart", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/ecommerce/abandoned-cart-reminders/cart-reminder-send/functionality.md", "start": 16, "end": 16, "fingerprint": "sha256:df49cec59730767d9d1fae2bb6dd820a69c12dde44e23233a60b0600fad543f4", "text": "- One click, one reminder, at most: the send key is built from the shop and cart, so a double-click, a second browser tab, a page reload or a retried request all resolve to the same attempt. The first one through decides; the rest show the same outcome, because a duplicate message is spam no matter how it was caused.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 19, "text": "\n## Rules & behavior\n- Who may click: only a signed-in owner or staff member of the shop that holds the cart. A click for another shop's cart, or from a signed-out session, is refused before anything else happens and nothing is recorded as a reminder, because no customer can be contacted on behalf of a shop the person does not act for.\n- One click, one reminder, at most: the send key is built from the shop and cart, so a double-click, a second browser tab, a page reload or a retried request all resolve to the same attempt. The first one through decides; the rest show the same outcome, because a duplicate message is spam no matter how it was caused.\n- Eligibility is checked at click time, never earlier: consent and the cart's state can change between the cart being listed and the owner's click, so the decision uses what is true at the moment of sending.\n- Blocked means nothing leaves the shop: on any blocked reason, no message is built or handed to delivery, the attempt is recorded as blocked with its reason, and the owner sees that reason.\n- Delivery failure is told, not hidden: if the notifications side refuses or cannot take the hand-off, the attempt is recorded as failed, the owner sees \"Not sent \u2014 delivery failed, try later\", and the cart is not marked reminded, so a later click can try again without breaking the one-per-cart rule."}}}, {"asked": "whether a failed send may be retried", "found": "failed attempt is recorded, cart not marked reminded, a later click can try again", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/ecommerce/abandoned-cart-reminders/cart-reminder-send/functionality.md", "start": 19, "end": 19, "fingerprint": "sha256:2fbc80caf818a3a1d781c571f4a6074d86c6b0edacbb95fc2a7dee6ac781a2e2", "text": "- Delivery failure is told, not hidden: if the notifications side refuses or cannot take the hand-off, the attempt is recorded as failed, the owner sees \"Not sent \u2014 delivery failed, try later\", and the cart is not marked reminded, so a later click can try again without breaking the one-per-cart rule.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 16, "end": 22, "text": "- One click, one reminder, at most: the send key is built from the shop and cart, so a double-click, a second browser tab, a page reload or a retried request all resolve to the same attempt. The first one through decides; the rest show the same outcome, because a duplicate message is spam no matter how it was caused.\n- Eligibility is checked at click time, never earlier: consent and the cart's state can change between the cart being listed and the owner's click, so the decision uses what is true at the moment of sending.\n- Blocked means nothing leaves the shop: on any blocked reason, no message is built or handed to delivery, the attempt is recorded as blocked with its reason, and the owner sees that reason.\n- Delivery failure is told, not hidden: if the notifications side refuses or cannot take the hand-off, the attempt is recorded as failed, the owner sees \"Not sent \u2014 delivery failed, try later\", and the cart is not marked reminded, so a later click can try again without breaking the one-per-cart rule.\n- The owner's view stays truthful: after a successful send the cart shows \"Reminded on <date>\" wherever the owner sees it, and the Remind action for that cart shows that state instead of sending again.\n- No extra effort: the action never asks the owner to confirm, choose a channel or edit text. Anything that would need a choice (for example, an offer) is out of scope at this stage.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-029", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "How long does the Reminder record keep its entries?", "answer": "Not set in any tier; the product owner decides (memory update mu-20261020-007). It must cover every month the win-back views show and recompute, so nothing is deleted until decided.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T05:03:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "which months the win-back views need", "found": "every month from the baseline month onward is shown", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/ecommerce/carts-won-back/owner-monthly-win-back/functionality.md", "start": 15, "end": 15, "fingerprint": "sha256:d06361757c65b9bd183c47e0c439a5b32526ae76807f982042ba768e9d3a68a7", "text": "- Every month from the baseline month onward is shown, including months where nothing was won back, because a missing month reads as \"no data\" and hides a bad month.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 12, "end": 18, "text": "\n## Rules & behavior\n- The owner sees only their own shop. A request for another shop's figures is refused, not filtered to empty, so a mistake in scoping cannot quietly show the wrong shop's numbers.\n- Every month from the baseline month onward is shown, including months where nothing was won back, because a missing month reads as \"no data\" and hides a bad month.\n- A month whose window has not yet passed is labelled \"still open \u2014 figures can still grow\", so the owner does not mistake an unfinished month for a drop.\n- The comparison with the baseline is total sales won back from abandoned carts in the month against the same total in the baseline month; the reminded part is shown beside it so the owner can see how much came after a reminder.\n- When the shop has no baseline, the comparison column says \"no baseline\" with the reason, and no difference or percentage is shown."}}}, {"asked": "retention guidance in the shelves", "found": "retention and deletion controls apply when compliance includes GDPR/HIPAA/SOC2; no length given", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/memory/knowledge/domains/analytics.md", "start": 83, "end": 83, "fingerprint": "sha256:982dc9dfcb841d2de4c1c15dec1a28520d317cfc5ccbc2f0f7b0f549e5aae3ee", "text": "  - Retention & deletion controls \u2014 TTLs and subject-deletion paths. Add when `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA / SOC2.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 80, "end": 86, "text": "- **Privacy-aware collection** \u2014 consent and minimisation where a regime applies.\n  - Consent gating \u2014 collect only after consent. The floor when `compliance` includes GDPR or `nfr.privacy >= medium`.\n  - Data minimisation & anonymisation \u2014 drop or hash PII, IP truncation. Add when `nfr.privacy >= high` or `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA.\n  - Retention & deletion controls \u2014 TTLs and subject-deletion paths. Add when `compliance` includes GDPR / HIPAA / SOC2.\n\n## Where it goes wrong (our gaps)\n- **Page-load + CTA only** \u2014 activity metrics with no goals or funnels \u2192 no value derived."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261020-030", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "What does the reminder message do when some or all cart items are unavailable, and how does it handle opt-out and the return link?", "answer": "Lists only available items and never promises stock; builds nothing when every item is unavailable (not cart-emptied, which the eligibility check blocks); every message carries a one-click opt-out; the link restores the same cart.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T05:03:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the cart reminder pattern", "found": "message with a link that restores the same cart; opt-in required at privacy medium or GDPR", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:758279c57f70d4f95e014931f0c4cefdde307dab095d65515c44cf910b130366", "text": "  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection \u2014 mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor \u2014 every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts \u2014 list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder \u2014 operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` \u2192 Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking \u2014 count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` \u2192 Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives \u2014 timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge \u2014 spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}, {"asked": "consent floor for reaching a person", "found": "opt-in / opt-out is the floor", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/memory/knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 84, "end": 84, "fingerprint": "sha256:07560b04e24486f012e86bc138ac9a9df32976ea39a539d49fad329d2d42d0f9", "text": "  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 81, "end": 87, "text": "  - Level 2 \u2014 in-session experience-nudge vs channel-bell: present \u2192 hand to `experience`'s nudge layer; away \u2192 fire the channel. Add when real-time presence signals are reliable.\n  - Level 3 \u2014 player-type tailoring: shape the nudge to gamified behaviour (progress/achievement/exploration/social). Add when `personalization` supplies a behavioural profile.\n- **Preferences & frequency** \u2014 let the user stay in control; never spam.\n  - Opt-in / opt-out \u2014 the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference \u2014 when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control \u2014 when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.\n"}}}, {"asked": "how an empty cart is handled", "found": "a cart with no items left is blocked as cart-emptied by the eligibility check", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/ecommerce/abandoned-cart-reminders/cart-reminder-eligibility/functionality.md", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:1fbae18ad026221d1b681d6f9a12d19e37abd88c2b941f828c4f891e0c8786b6", "text": "- Cart state is read live: a cart that has since ended in an order is blocked as cart-ordered, and one with no items left is blocked as cart-emptied, because reminding someone about a purchase they already made, or a cart they cleared, is noise.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 21, "text": "- No contact: a cart with no customer contact (for example a guest who never gave an email address) is blocked as no-contact, because there is nobody the shop may reach.\n- Consent fails closed: only a current, unwithdrawn opt-in to hear from this shop allows a reminder. Never asked, withdrawn and unknown all block, and a failure to read the consent records also blocks, because guessing yes is the one failure this capability must never have.\n- Consent is per shop: an opt-in given to one shop on the platform never counts for another, because the customer agreed to hear from that shop, not from the platform.\n- Cart state is read live: a cart that has since ended in an order is blocked as cart-ordered, and one with no items left is blocked as cart-emptied, because reminding someone about a purchase they already made, or a cart they cleared, is noise.\n- One per cart: any earlier sent reminder for this cart blocks as already-reminded with its date. A blocked or failed attempt does not count as sent, so it never uses up the cart's one reminder.\n- Per-customer limit: if this customer received a sent reminder from this shop within the last 7 days, for any cart, the check blocks as customer-limit and says when the window ends. Seven days is the proposed default awaiting the owner's confirmation; the window is a single setting so it can change without changing the rule.\n- The check never sends, writes or changes anything; it only reads and answers, so it can be run safely as often as needed."}}}], "from_update": null}], "problems": []}
