here it goes wrong\n- **Fatigue & noise** — too many low-value messages; no frequency discipline."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261020-011", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Where in the knowledge base does 'Seeing today's abandoned carts' belong?", "answer": "ecommerce -> Abandoned-cart recovery (the approved shelf addition), resting on Inventory & order management Level 1", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:55:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "which domain's trigger covers carts and orders", "found": "ecommerce is the only shelf whose trigger names cart and orders", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 5, "end": 5, "fingerprint": "sha256:6b5ec069a363310f568b9f09f8c68e1dd5b35b45df74d5879cd69dcfbcd0301d", "text": "  trigger: \"the product sells physical or digital goods — catalog, cart, orders, storefront\"", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 2, "end": 8, "text": "id: domains/ecommerce\ntitle: \"Ecommerce: how we build it — content-first MACH, selected on the commerce↔content spectrum\"\nconditions:\n  trigger: \"the product sells physical or digital goods — catalog, cart, orders, storefront\"\n  selection_keys: [commerce-vs-content-weight, sku-count, traffic-volume, merchandising-depth, nfr.performance]\nprovenance: interview (#434) + an eCommerce selection-criterion reference\n---"}}}, {"asked": "a capability on the shelf that owns seeing abandoned carts", "found": "the approved addition Abandoned-cart recovery makes those carts visible to the operator", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 1, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:13e9593ced352e2eb52627ae3520ac07810ece177b8fd5fb5319d0dfaae7728d", "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 11, "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR."}}}, {"asked": "the records the view is built on", "found": "Inventory & order management Level 1 keeps basic stock and order records", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 125, "end": 127, "fingerprint": "sha256:e02d1822f9e9902bc4aec262f260122b9f486c6368d06c611477a8fde7d0dc61", "text": "- **Inventory & order management** — core commerce; real-time stock when traffic\n  and reliability push (quadrants 3–4).\n  - Level 1 — basic stock & orders: simple counts and order records. The floor — every store that sells.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 122, "end": 130, "text": "  - Ratings & written reviews — collect and display buyer feedback. The floor when shoppers evaluate before buying.\n  - Moderation & verified-purchase — gate UGC and mark genuine buyers. Add when `shape.users: public` invites abuse, or `compliance` needs records.\n  - Review intelligence — AI summaries and consumer review Q&A on the PDP (see intelligence). Add for public, conversion-focused storefronts.\n- **Inventory & order management** — core commerce; real-time stock when traffic\n  and reliability push (quadrants 3–4).\n  - Level 1 — basic stock & orders: simple counts and order records. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Level 2 — real-time stock & reservations: live availability under load. Add when `nfr.reliability >= high` and `nfr.performance >= high` (quadrants 3–4).\n  - Level 3 — distributed / omnichannel fulfilment: multi-warehouse, BOPIS, returns. Add when `shape.surfaces` spans channels or `nfr.scalability >= xhigh`.\n- **Integration / SOA layer** — heavy for quadrant 4: many back-end systems,"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261020-012", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Which functionalities does the capability break into?", "answer": "Abandoned-cart detection and Today's abandoned-carts list", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:55:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "how a cart becomes abandoned", "found": "mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 9, "end": 9, "fingerprint": "sha256:03dd04430213715ba73034e24b03b316f0a19c8828734695c55160a98a78a811", "text": "  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 12, "text": "  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking — count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` → Goals, Funnels)."}}}, {"asked": "what the owner sees", "found": "list the carts abandoned in a period such as today with shopper, items and value", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 10, "end": 10, "fingerprint": "sha256:56fc764db48d724eb8f1147f0894678b458f3ee6c184d5d638859190e4a53551", "text": "  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 7, "end": 13, "text": "  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking — count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` → Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives — timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261020-013", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Where are the capability's edges with its neighbours?", "answer": "It shows carts only; reminding is abandoned-cart-reminders and counting win-backs is carts-won-back", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:55:45Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who sends the message and who measures the win-back", "found": "sending is notifications, measuring is analytics; the recovery capability owns which cart and when", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 1, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:13e9593ced352e2eb52627ae3520ac07810ece177b8fd5fb5319d0dfaae7728d", "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 11, "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR."}}}, {"asked": "which owner intent the view serves", "found": "the operator's Understand intent, learning from behaviour", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 38, "end": 41, "fingerprint": "sha256:edaf4ef3cddcea0a06c94bac8b38293faf3c0d3277d31db9645d2c972c5c22e2", "text": "**Operator (business) intents**\n- **Merchandise** — \"present and prioritise the catalog\" → merchandising, PLP curation.\n- **Enrich** — \"make products rich and on-brand\" → product content, brand-tone.\n- **Understand** — \"learn from behaviour and reviews\" → analytics, review analysis.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 35, "end": 44, "text": "- **Track & manage** — \"where is it / change or return it\" → order status, returns, reorder.\n- **Be assisted** — \"shop with help\" → agentic / conversational commerce.\n\n**Operator (business) intents**\n- **Merchandise** — \"present and prioritise the catalog\" → merchandising, PLP curation.\n- **Enrich** — \"make products rich and on-brand\" → product content, brand-tone.\n- **Understand** — \"learn from behaviour and reviews\" → analytics, review analysis.\n- **Operate** — \"keep stock and orders flowing\" → inventory, fulfilment.\n\n## Pick the shape first (the commerce↔content spectrum — our POV)"}}}], "from_update": null}
