+{"citation_id": "cite-20261020-016", "issue": 1, "play": "understand", "question": "Where does the abandoned-cart-reminders capability belong in the knowledge base?", "answer": "ecommerce -> Abandoned-cart recovery -> Cart reminder, using notifications for consent, frequency and email delivery", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-20T04:56:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "a home for one-click cart reminders", "found": "approved node: Cart reminder, operator-triggered, restores the same cart, opt-in where privacy >= medium", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1/context/answers/kb/ecommerce-abandoned-cart-recovery.md", "start": 1, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:5ee34f5e93d8792c47a497af99811c3df6d808150cc71174ead45477ae90f8f8", "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 14, "text": "- **Abandoned-cart recovery** — win back the sales a shopper started and left.\n  A cart that holds items but ends with no order is a lost sale the operator can\n  still recover; the capability makes those carts visible to the operator and\n  brings the shopper back to finish. It serves the shopper's *Acquire* intent\n  (\"let me buy it\") when it broke off, and the operator's *Understand* intent.\n  Sending the message is `notifications` (channel delivery, consent, frequency);\n  measuring the win-back is `analytics` (conversion funnel); this capability owns\n  the decision of WHICH cart, WHEN, and the way back into the same cart.\n  - Abandoned-cart detection — mark a cart abandoned when it holds items and no order follows within a set window. The floor — every store that sells.\n  - Operator view of abandoned carts — list the carts abandoned in a period (e.g. today) with shopper, items and value, so the operator knows which sales could still be won back. The floor wherever an operator runs the store.\n  - Cart reminder — operator-triggered (one click) or automatic message to the shopper that their cart is waiting, with a link that restores the same cart. Add when the shopper can be reached away from the store (`notifications` → Channel delivery); requires opt-in where `nfr.privacy >= medium` or `compliance` includes GDPR.\n  - Recovery tracking — count reminded carts that end in an order and the sales won back, over time. Add when the business sets a win-back goal (`analytics` → Goals, Funnels).\n  - Reminder sequences & incentives — timed follow-ups and an optional offer (next-best-offer / personalised promotion). Add when `shape.stage` is public/monetized and fatigue control is in place.\n  - Abandonment prediction & in-session nudge — spot a cart likely to be abandoned and nudge while the shopper is still present (`experience` governed nudges). Add when real-time presence signals are reliable (the shelf's core *Acquire* intelligence line)."}}}, {"asked": "which ecommerce intent a reminder serves", "found": "shopper Acquire intent: cart and checkout handoff", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 34, "end": 34, "fingerprint": "sha256:6a005cc38f5849c37f52a233f2c3f3f81e3eb757123db7c4a5a4128d702c1b3b", "text": "- **Acquire** — \"let me buy it\" → cart, checkout handoff.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 31, "end": 37, "text": "**Shopper intents**\n- **Discover** — \"help me find what I want\" → browse, category, PLP, search.\n- **Evaluate** — \"help me decide\" → PDP, reviews & ratings, recommendations, compare.\n- **Acquire** — \"let me buy it\" → cart, checkout handoff.\n- **Track & manage** — \"where is it / change or return it\" → order status, returns, reorder.\n- **Be assisted** — \"shop with help\" → agentic / conversational commerce.\n"}}}, {"asked": "consent and frequency for any message", "found": "opt-in/opt-out floor; fatigue/frequency control", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/notifications.md", "start": 83, "end": 86, "fingerprint": "sha256:a5922243ecc1a8df3a44b3e4ae04245bd64f9d0db59ac8b88abdebea7c789c42", "text": "- **Preferences & frequency** — let the user stay in control; never spam.\n  - Opt-in / opt-out — the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference — when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control — when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.", "version": "db6441a93356", "around": {"start": 80, "end": 89, "text": "  - Level 1 — presence detection: is the person in-session right now (the floor for routing at all).\n  - Level 2 — in-session experience-nudge vs channel-bell: present → hand to `experience`'s nudge layer; away → fire the channel. Add when real-time presence signals are reliable.\n  - Level 3 — player-type tailoring: shape the nudge to gamified behaviour (progress/achievement/exploration/social). Add when `personalization` supplies a behavioural profile.\n- **Preferences & frequency** — let the user stay in control; never spam.\n  - Opt-in / opt-out — the floor; consent to be reached at all (`nfr.privacy >= medium`, or `compliance` includes GDPR).\n  - Per-channel preference — when more than one channel exists, so the user picks where each message type lands.\n  - Fatigue / frequency control — when message volume rises, or `shape.stage` is public/monetized; cap low-value sends to protect attention.\n\n## Where it goes wrong\n- **Fatigue & noise** — too many low-value messages; no frequency discipline."}}}], "from_update": null}
